# producer.bot -- tests/threads.test: thread entries that send numbered
# notes to a mailbox of another VM through a Remote capability
# (transport.bot). produce retries a Full send itself; deliver_notes waits
# for room on its own event loop, woken through its port.
import event_loop_linux
import std::actor::remote
import std::event_loop
import std::thread

struct Note:
    from: int
    seq: int

struct Plan:
    who: int
    count: int
    to: std::actor::remote::Remote[Note]

# Sends COUNT notes to the plan's mailbox, retrying a Full one at once:
# how many were refused for room.
thread fn produce(plan: Plan) -> int:
    fold i from 0 to plan.count with intermediate full 0:
        tries = fold with intermediate t 0:
            sent = std::actor::remote::send(plan.to, Note {from: plan.who, seq: i})
            if sent == std::actor::remote::Sent::Delivered:
                break
            t + 1
        full + tries

# The plan's notes from a task of this VM's loop: a Full endpoint suspends
# the task until the transport rings the port with room. How many were
# delivered; the port closed after the last.
fn delivering(plan: Plan, context ev: std::event_loop::Loop, p: std::thread::Port, db: std::thread::Doorbell) -> int errors std::event_loop::TaskFailed, IndexNotFound, std::event_loop::SchedulerFault, std::event_loop::DriverFault:
    n = fold i from 0 to plan.count with intermediate n 0:
        sent = std::actor::remote::deliver(plan.to, Note {from: plan.who, seq: i})
        if sent != std::actor::remote::Sent::Delivered:
            break
        n + 1
    std::thread::close_port()
    n

private fn delivered(plan: Plan, context ev: std::event_loop::Loop, d: std::event_loop::Driver, p: std::thread::Port, db: std::thread::Doorbell) -> int errors std::event_loop::SchedulerFault, std::event_loop::DriverFault, std::event_loop::LoopReentered:
    std::thread::serve()
    coroutine {step, first} = delivering(plan)
    task = std::event_loop::adopt(step, first)
    std::event_loop::run()
    fold o in std::event_loop::take_outcomes() with intermediate n 0:
        if o.task == task:
            o.value
        else:
            n

thread fn deliver_notes(plan: Plan) -> int:
    with context std::event_loop::create(16)
    with context event_loop_linux::create()
    with context event_loop_linux::native()
    with context std::thread::port()
    delivered(plan):
        on std::event_loop::SchedulerFault:
            -1
        on std::event_loop::DriverFault {code}:
            code
        on std::event_loop::LoopReentered:
            -2
